{
  "comment": "Same plugin-panel pattern as d110/jv1080. The U-110 edit buffer is the temporary PATCH: common (name in the name field, output mode, chorus/tremolo) + 6 parts. Every part group shares one select var {n} (select.shared = 'part', 'all' writes all six parts). Part groups follow the manual's Part Setting groups: basic (tone pick = media + number, output assign, receive channel, program change + map, key range), level (level, velocity, attack/release offsets, aftertouch), pitch (coarse/fine shift, bend range, detune, poly aftertouch), LFO (rate, auto delay/rise/depth, manual rise/depth, aftertouch). The tone is chosen as media (INT or card C01-C15) + number 1-99; names live in schema.tones (a 'tone' display keyed on toneLookup.mediaKey would show them).",
